# #5837, the claimless advance: a split resumed by a new donor activation (a5e2e2ef).
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestResumedCloseOwnHighOldTokenNotStale
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: both: the resumed close uses only its own high, and the old activation's records are not stale
PERTURBS: DonorRestart
BOUNDS: WithFreeAdvance = TRUE, WithSplitBirth = TRUE, WithDonorRestart = TRUE, WithKeyMove = TRUE, MaxWindows = 1, WithMixedVersion = FALSE, WithDuplicate = FALSE

--- FIND
DonorCloseCovers == IF dResumed THEN {o \in Offs : author[o] = DonorLive} ELSE dKnown
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the resumed close uses only the new activation's own high.
DonorCloseCovers == dKnown
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ sHi' = Max({sHi} \cup {o \in Offs : author[o] = DonorLive})
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the old activation's token is still counted as live.
    /\ UNCHANGED sHi
--- END
